    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0186" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg96"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1445</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vologda</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-04T16:00:00+02:31"><hi rendition="#italic">April 4, 1918,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 6, 8.59 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. Have seen Consul General’s cable No. 303, March 31,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d136-f1"/> to-day. Robins
                    forwards me daily reports from Webster in Irkutsk but [who]
                        <pb facs="0187" n="97" xml:id="pg97"/> proceeding Chita with British officer
                    and Soviet representative. They say Bolsheviks protesting against Semenov<anchor n="1" xml:id="d136-f2"/> in the
                    Siberian raids on Chinese territory and against assistance rendered by Allies.
                        Semenov says only endeavoring to
                    restore order in Siberia.
                        Webster-Hicks’s reports give
                    different impression about conditions along Siberia from those of consuls.</p>
                <p>Russian Government telegraphed Siberian Soviet and local Soviet and railroad
                    officials to protect and expedite railway engineers <hi rendition="#italic">en
                        route</hi> Vologda and says experienced railroad official requested will be
                    sent Vologda when time specified.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
